      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"status\": \"partial\",\n  \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n  \"useful_material\": [\n    \"该综述明确指出目前缺乏针对肌苷在结直肠癌（CRC）发生过程中不同肠道 compartment 空间分布的临床研究，现有数据多源于“批量代谢组学分析”（bulk metabolomic analysis），未提供标准化的绝对浓度测量协议。\",\n    \"文中提到目前没有人研究纵向追踪从结肠炎到异型增生再到确诊 CRC 过程中的肌苷水平或嘌呤代谢通量，表明缺乏标准化的纵向监测方案。\",\n    \"引用了一项 II 期临床试验（n=172），其中肌苷作为免疫治疗辅助（0.2 g 口服，每日三次），但未单独报告 CRC 亚组结果，且未提及血清或肿瘤微环境中内源性肌苷的基线测量标准或参考范围。\",\n    \"指出肌苷在人体 CRC 患者中的特征描述相比其他代谢物（如胆汁酸、SCFAs）仍不足，暗示该领域尚未形成统一的测量或报告共识。\"\n  ],\n  \"auxiliary_material\": [\n    \"提供了肌苷的化学性质（分子式、稳定性、pH 敏感性），这对理解测量时的样本处理条件（如避免酸性水解或氧化降解）有潜在参考价值。\",\n    \"列举了产生肌苷的特定细菌 taxa（如 Bifidobacterium pseudolongum, Lactobacillus spp.），可作为未来标准化测量中关联微生物组数据的背景信息。\",\n    \"描述了肌苷通过 A2A 受体调节免疫的机制，以及其在肿瘤微环境中作为替代碳源的作用，有助于解释为何需要标准化测量其浓度以评估治疗效果。\",\n    \"提到工程菌和补充剂疗法的挑战（如药代动力学、最佳剂量），间接说明缺乏标准化浓度测量会阻碍剂量 - 反应关系的确定。\"\n  ],\n  \"remaining_gap\": \"该材料确认了领域内缺乏针对人体肿瘤微环境或血清中肌苷绝对浓度测量的共识指南或标准化协议。具体缺失包括： compartment 特异性（肠腔 vs. 组织）的采样标准、纵向监测方案、以及临床参考范围。虽然提到了批量代谢组学的使用，但未说明具体的分析平台或定量方法是否已标准化。\",\n  \"outline_action\": \"在综述的‘方法学挑战’或‘未来方向’部分，引用此材料作为证据，说明当前微生物代谢物（特别是肌苷）临床测量的异质性和标准化缺失。建议后续行动包括：1) 检索具体的代谢组学方法学论文以寻找可能使用的 LC-MS/MS 等具体技术参数；2) 关注正在进行的临床试验方案（protocol）是否公开了生物标志物测量细节；3) 将肌苷的测量现状与已有标准化方法的代谢物（如 SCFAs）进行对比，突出紧迫性。\"\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to analyze a provided paper text against a specific gap question about standardized methods for measuring metabolite concentrations (like inosine, SCFAs) in human tumor microenvironment or serum.\n\n**Gap Question:** \"是否有共识指南或标准化方法用于人体肿瘤微环境或血清中关键代谢物（如肌苷、SCFAs）的绝对浓度测量？\" (Are there consensus guidelines or standardized methods for absolute concentration measurement of key metabolites (e.g., inosine, SCFAs) in human tumor microenvironment or serum?)\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n1. Find specific standardized measurement protocols, reference ranges, or consensus statements.\n2. Or confirm the status remains 'partial' (i.e., no consensus exists).\n\n**Material Reading Text:** A review article about Inosine, its role in gut homeostasis, and CRC. It discusses mechanisms, sources, signaling, and some clinical trial data (one phase-2 trial).\n\n**Review Planning B:** Provides context on how this review fits into a broader literature planning effort (microbiome & ICI). It highlights mechanisms, clinical gaps, and comparisons.\n\n**Task:**\n1. Describe what the study (this review) studied and found.\n2. Explain how that material helps with the requested gap.\n3. Assign status (fulfilled, partial, unmet, unjudgeable).\n4. Assign material_usefulness (direct, supporting, none).\n5. Fill useful_material, auxiliary_material, remaining_gap, outline_action.\n6. Follow strict constraints (JSON output, no quotation ledger, specific phrasing, etc.).\n\n**Analysis of the Text regarding the Gap:**\n- The gap asks for *standardized measurement protocols*, *reference ranges*, or *consensus guidelines* for absolute concentration of metabolites (inosine, SCFAs) in human tumor/serum.\n- The text is a *review article* summarizing biological roles, mechanisms, and some clinical trial outcomes.\n- Section 4.1 mentions: \"Unfortunately, studies reporting the effects of the spatial redistribution of inosine across different intestinal compartments along 